Today’s topic was RAG. Here’s my understanding:
learned about a RAG 
basic and very importent concept , where it produces a answers or solutions from external sources through retrival 
🔹 LLMs only know what they were trained on, so they can give outdated or wrong answers.
🔹 RAG first retrieves relevant information from external data (documents, PDFs, databases), then passes it to the LLM to generate the answer.
🔹 It’s like an open-book exam instead of answering from memory.

